perf: exclude large slices from IPC state sync to main process

The store.subscribe handler sends the entire Redux state to the main
process via IPC every 100ms. When messageBlocks contains large data
(e.g. base64 images from tool responses), serializing and transferring
this state blocks the main thread for 200-500ms per cycle — longer
than the 100ms throttle interval — causing the UI to freeze
continuously.

Exclude `messages` and `messageBlocks` from the IPC payload. These
slices are already blacklisted from Redux Persist and are never read
by the main process (verified: ReduxService.selectSync/stateCache has
no consumers that access message or block data). The main process only
needs lightweight slices like settings, assistants, and llm configs.
